 Successful writes return `{ "status": "ok" }`.
+
+### Conditional deletion (PostgreSQL)
+
+`DELETE /v8/management/credentials/conditional?id=<UUID>` and
+`DELETE /v8/management/channel-group-details/<ID>/conditional` require
+`If-Match: "<sha256>"`, the lowercase SHA-256 of the selected database row's
+PostgreSQL `to_jsonb(row)::text` UTF-8 bytes. Home locks the row, compares that
+checksum, and runs its normal soft deletion in the same transaction. A changed
+or missing row returns `412 {"error":"precondition_failed"}` without deletion.
+An invalid checksum returns 400. Other databases refuse this operation. The
+ordinary ID-only deletion routes keep their existing behavior.
